# React Frontend

## Folder structure (mandatory)

```
src/
├── Features/     # Page/route features (UI + local context + subcomponents)
├── Shared/       # Reusable UI, utils, websocket client
└── Domain/       # React Query hooks per entity (HTTP/WS isolated here)
```

Example: `Features/Auction/`, `Domain/Auction/hooks/useAuction.ts`.

## Component file conventions

Colocate in the same directory when applicable:

- `Component.tsx` — component
- `Component.types.ts` — props/types
- `Component.styles.scss` — scoped styles
- `Component.test.ts` — tests (Vitest)

Subcomponents live under `components/`; feature utils under `utils/`; local state in `contexts/`.

## Data & real-time

- **All API calls** via React Query hooks in `Domain/{Entity}/hooks/` — never fetch directly from feature components.
- **WebSocket:** single shared client at `Shared/websocket/socketClient.ts`; subscribe by topic, don't create per-feature clients.
- Real-time features (events, auctions, logs, balance) subscribe through Domain hooks or a thin wrapper around `socketClient`.

## Styling

- SCSS only; **central theme** at `Shared/styles/theme.scss` — use variables for colors, never hardcode palette in components.
- Import component styles as `Component.styles.scss` alongside the `.tsx`.
- **Visual language:** RF Online client windows — chamfered metal panels, title bars, inventory slots, hazard stripes. No rounded corners, no glowing text, no grid backgrounds.
- **Typography:** `$font-family` (Barlow Semi Condensed) for body/labels/inputs — never below 16px (`$font-size-base`). `$font-heading` (Big Shoulders Display) for titles, nav, buttons — use `$font-size-ui` (16px) or larger, uppercase with short tracking (0.5–1px). `$font-mono` (Share Tech Mono) for points, timers, bids, IDs — never below 14px (`$font-size-heading`). Use `$font-size-section` (20px) or larger for prominent titles.
- **Building blocks:** wrap page sections in the shared `Panel` component (`Shared/ui/components/Panel`). Mixins in `theme.scss`: `panel` / `panel-titlebar` (windows), `card` (sub-panel), `slot` (icons/items), `readout` (numeric displays), `tag` (small technical labels), `hazard-stripe` (admin/danger), `chamfer` / `chamfer-edges` (cut corners), `field-input` / `field-label` (forms).
